  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On September 1, CENTCOM confirmed airstrikes on IRGC Aerospace Force positions at Qeshm and Jask, the largest US direct action inside Iranian territory since the June escalation. Within hours, Iran's IRGC launched a ballistic missile salvo toward US-allied assets in Jordan and the UAE, confirmed by CENTCOM and UK NAVCENT. The exchange simultaneously resolved two forecasts: F8 (strike pause by Sep 14) as RESOLVED-NO, and set the foundation for new forecast F9 at 60% for IRGC follow-on retaliation by Sep 5. → moved <span class="cite">F8</span>, <span class="cite">F9</span></p>

      <p>Hormuz transit data from Lloyd's List for Sep 1-2 recorded approximately 13 AIS-confirmed commercial vessels per 24-hour period, below the prior USNI figure of 16.3/day from Aug 28. The discrepancy was resolved by the Judge in favour of Lloyd's List as operationally specific and more recent; the USNI figure likely included naval vessels over a partial measurement period. The current 13/day baseline is 46% below the 24/day threshold required for F4, against 43 days remaining on the horizon and an active military exchange. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>Iran's MFA produced no formal written statement on Hormuz preconditions by the Sep 2 resolution deadline for F1. IRGC and Khamenei office statements on conditions for reopening were repeated during the period but do not satisfy the F1 criterion (which requires MFA-specific formal text). F1 resolved NO at p=0.10 at horizon. F2 (formal deal by Sep 14) was moved to the 5% schema floor following F1's NO and the Sep 1 military exchange: the gating prerequisite and the diplomatic track are both absent for this window. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span>, <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>The IAEA Director-General issued an 'urgent need' statement on Sep 1-2 and confirmed Iran's inspector access status as 'unclear'. This followed the Aug 26 Iran AEOI Chief formal blocking doctrine barring inspections of war-damaged sites pending new protocol agreement. Both findings were independently confirmed by Analyst and DA agents; Judge resolved the divergence (Analyst 0.22, DA ~0.10) at F3 = 0.11, anchoring to the structural blocking doctrine as the primary constraint. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>Two new forecasts were added today. F9 (IRGC Gulf retaliation by Sep 5, 60%, military) was created to track the near-term retaliation cycle following Sep 1 strikes. F10 (Oman mediation active by Sep 14, 15%, diplomacy) was created to track Oman's historical back-channel role as a potential pressure valve; at 15%, the forecast captures Oman's established channel against Iran's expected post-strike refusal window of 10-30 days. → moved <span class="cite">F9</span>, <span class="cite">F10</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

